  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why the gate has four conditions",
      "items": [
        "AICore rejects payloads over roughly 4K tokens rather than truncating them",
        "Nano holds one session, so a second concurrent turn returns BUSY",
        "AICore deprioritises background callers, so a backgrounded app can stall"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The fallback is not a failure",
      "items": [
        "Both paths return the same shape, so callers never branch on where it ran",
        "FeatureStatus can be UNAVAILABLE while the model downloads, on a device that will support it later",
        "Falling through to cloud keeps the reply shape identical, so callers do not branch",
        "Without an API key the cloud path returns a system message saying so, never a fabricated answer"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
